#ASSERT `s 278.12(2) the application may be made to a judge, provincial court judge or justice presiding at any other proceedings` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 278.12: the accused's application (lines 5315-5342)`

-- (3): fields: in writing, particulars, the thing sought is a therapeutic record, grounds for a record, grounds for a therapeutic record
#ASSERT `s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(3) the application meets the requirements of form and content` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE


#ASSERT `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` (LIST `s 278.12(4)(a) that the record or therapeutic record exists`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` (LIST `s 278.12(4)(a) that the record or therapeutic record exists`, `s 278.12(4)(b) that the record or therapeutic record relates to medical or psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling that the complainant or witness has received or is receiving`, `s 278.12(4)(c) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the incident that is the subject matter of the proceedings`, `s 278.12(4)(d) that the record or therapeutic record may disclose a prior inconsistent statement of the complainant or witness`, `s 278.12(4)(e) that the record or therapeutic record may relate to the credibility of the complainant or witness`, `s 278.12(4)(f) that the record or therapeutic record may relate to the reliability of the testimony of the complainant or witness merely because the complainant or witness has received or is receiving psychiatric treatment, therapy or counselling`, `s 278.12(4)(g) that the record or therapeutic record may reveal allegations of sexual abuse of the complainant by a person other than the accused`, `s 278.12(4)(h) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the sexual activity of the complainant with any person, including the accused`, `s 278.12(4)(i) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the presence or absence of a recent complaint`, `s 278.12(4)(j) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the complainant's sexual reputation`, `s 278.12(4)(k) that the record or therapeutic record was made close in time to a complaint or to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` (LIST `s 278.12(4)(k) that the record or therapeutic record was made close in time to a complaint or to the activity that forms the subject matter of the charge against the accused`, `s 278.12(4)(c) that the record or therapeutic record relates to the incident that is the subject matter of the proceedings`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` (LIST `s 278.12(4)(a) that the record or therapeutic record exists`, `s 278.12(4) any other assertion`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` (LIST `s 278.12(4) any other assertion`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 278.12(4) the assertions are not sufficient on their own to establish likely relevance or a reasonable doubt` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

